{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BREADCRUMB
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Custom addition to the Impact theme, not part of Maestrooo's base code. Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid so every
page gets the same trail, instead of editing each main-* section and fighting them on the next theme update.

********************************************
Where the hierarchy comes from, on a product
********************************************

Home > game and language > format > product. Both middle levels are derived from data already carried by the product,
so the trail is identical whatever page the shopper came from, and identical to what Googlebot sees when it fetches the
canonical URL with no referrer. That stability is the whole point: structured data that changes with the referrer is
worse than no structured data.

  Level 2, the aisle    accessories       -> 'accessoires'
                        anything else     -> '<game>-<language>', falling back to '<game>' alone
  Level 3, the format   accessories       -> vcollect.type_accessoire
                        anything else     -> product.type

The slug tables below are the only place a value is translated into a collection handle. A game, language, accessory
type or product type that is missing from them simply produces no crumb at that level, it never produces a wrong one.

Both levels are then confirmed against product.collections before being rendered. That check does two things at once:
it proves the product really belongs to the collection it points at, and, since product.collections excludes anything
not published to the Online Store, it proves the URL is reachable. A candidate that fails is dropped and the next one
is tried. So the One Piece display resolves to 'one-piece' at level 2 and to nothing at level 3, because the automated
'displays' collection is scoped to Pokémon and does not contain it.

********************************************
Where the hierarchy comes from, elsewhere
********************************************

Shopify collections are a flat list, there is no parent/child relation to read. On a collection page the only place the
catalogue is organised in levels is the navigation menu, so the parent level is looked up in the main menu: a collection
that appears as a sub-item of "Boosters et packs" gets that entry inserted before it.

Consequence to keep in mind: re-organising the main menu re-organises the breadcrumb of the collection pages. That is
intended, it keeps a single place to maintain. A collection absent from the menu simply has no parent level.

The menu handle is hardcoded to 'main-menu' because the header reads its menu from a section setting, which a layout
snippet cannot access. Verified in sections/header-group.json: the header is set to "main-menu".

********************************************
Structured data
********************************************

This snippet emits the BreadcrumbList JSON-LD itself, from the exact same variables it renders, so what a shopper reads
and what Google indexes can never drift. The BreadcrumbList that Impact used to emit in snippets/microdata-schema.liquid
was removed for that reason: two BreadcrumbList on one page compete, and that one ignored the parent level.

********************************************
Placement note
********************************************

This renders before the first section inside <main>, so `[role="main"] .shopify-section:first-child` no longer matches
and `--section-is-first` stays 0. That variable is read only by the transparent-header rules (theme.css line 842 and the
`allow_transparent_header` blocks in collection-banner, image-with-text-overlay, main-article, main-blog, slideshow and
video). `allow_transparent_header` is false on every template of this store, verified on 21/07/2026, so nothing changes
today. If a first section is ever switched to a transparent header, hide the breadcrumb on that page, otherwise the
section is pulled up by the header height and covers it.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign show_breadcrumb = true

  case request.page_type
    when 'index', 'password', 'captcha', 'gift_card'
      assign show_breadcrumb = false
  endcase

  case request.page_type
    when 'product'
      assign current_title = product.title
    when 'collection'
      assign current_title = collection.title
    when 'blog'
      assign current_title = blog.title
    when 'article'
      assign current_title = article.title
    when 'page'
      assign current_title = page.title
    when 'cart'
      assign current_title = 'cart.general.title' | t
    when 'search'
      assign current_title = 'search.general.title' | t
    when '404'
      assign current_title = '404.general.title' | t
    else
      assign current_title = page_title
  endcase

  assign crumb_aisle = null
  assign crumb_format = null

  if request.page_type == 'product'
    assign product_game = product.metafields.vcollect.tcg.value
    assign product_language = product.metafields.vcollect.langue.value
    assign accessory_type = product.metafields.vcollect.type_accessoire.value

    assign game_slug = ''
    case product_game
      when 'Pokémon'
        assign game_slug = 'pokemon'
      when 'One Piece'
        assign game_slug = 'one-piece'
    endcase

    assign language_slug = ''
    case product_language
      when 'Japonais'
        assign language_slug = 'japonais'
      when 'Français'
        assign language_slug = 'francais'
      when 'Chinois'
        assign language_slug = 'chinois'
      when 'Anglais'
        assign language_slug = 'anglais'
    endcase

    comment
      Candidates are ordered from the most specific to the least, joined into a string because Liquid cannot append to
      an array. Accessories never carry a language, they get their own aisle.
    endcomment

    assign aisle_candidates = ''

    if accessory_type != blank or product.type == 'Accessoire'
      assign aisle_candidates = 'accessoires'
    elsif game_slug != ''
      assign aisle_candidates = game_slug
      if language_slug != ''
        assign aisle_candidates = game_slug | append: '-' | append: language_slug | append: ',' | append: game_slug
      endif
    endif

    assign format_candidate = ''
    case accessory_type
      when 'Classeur'
        assign format_candidate = 'classeurs'
      when 'Toploaders'
        assign format_candidate = 'toploaders'
      when 'Sleeves'
        assign format_candidate = 'sleeves'
      when 'Protection acrylique'
        assign format_candidate = 'protections-acryliques'
    endcase

    if format_candidate == ''
      case product.type
        when 'Display'
          assign format_candidate = 'displays'
        when 'Booster'
          assign format_candidate = 'boosters'
        when 'Coffret'
          assign format_candidate = 'coffrets'
        when 'ETB'
          assign format_candidate = 'etb'
        when 'Tripack'
          assign format_candidate = 'tripacks'
        when 'Blister'
          assign format_candidate = 'blisters'
      endcase
    endif

    comment
      A candidate is kept only if the product actually belongs to it. product.collections lists the collections the
      product is in that are published to the Online Store, so this validates the membership and the URL in one pass.
    endcomment

    if aisle_candidates != ''
      assign aisle_candidates = aisle_candidates | split: ','

      for candidate in aisle_candidates
        for product_collection in product.collections
          if product_collection.handle == candidate
            assign crumb_aisle = product_collection
            break
          endif
        endfor

        if crumb_aisle != null
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif

    if format_candidate != '' and format_candidate != crumb_aisle.handle
      for product_collection in product.collections
        if product_collection.handle == format_candidate
          assign crumb_format = product_collection
          break
        endif
      endfor
    endif
  endif

  comment
    Collection pages keep their own rule: the parent level is the entry the collection sits under in the main menu.
  endcomment

  assign parent_title = ''
  assign parent_url = ''

  if request.page_type == 'collection' and collection.url != blank and collection.handle != 'all'
    for top_link in linklists['main-menu'].links
      if top_link.url == collection.url
        break
      endif

      for child_link in top_link.links
        if child_link.url == collection.url
          assign parent_title = top_link.title
          assign parent_url = top_link.url
          break
        endif
      endfor

      if parent_title != ''
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}

{%- if show_breadcrumb and current_title != blank -%}
  <style>
    .breadcrumb {
      padding-block: var(--spacing-4);
    }

    .breadcrumb__list {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--spacing-2);
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .breadcrumb__item {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--spacing-2);
      min-width: 0;
    }

    .breadcrumb__link {
      color: rgb(var(--text-color) / 0.7);
      text-decoration: none;
      transition: color 0.2s ease-in-out;
    }

    .breadcrumb__link:hover {
      color: rgb(var(--text-color));
    }

    .breadcrumb__separator {
      color: rgb(var(--text-color) / 0.4);
      flex: none;
    }

    /* Long product titles must fold instead of pushing the trail out of the container */
    .breadcrumb__current {
      color: rgb(var(--text-color));
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }
  </style>

  <nav class="breadcrumb container" aria-label="{{ 'general.accessibility.breadcrumb' | t }}">
    <ol class="breadcrumb__list text-sm">
      <li class="breadcrumb__item">
        <a class="breadcrumb__link" href="{{ routes.root_url }}">{{ 'general.home' | t }}</a>
        {%- render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-right-small', class: 'breadcrumb__separator', direction_aware: true -%}
      </li>

      {%- if parent_url != '' -%}
        <li class="breadcrumb__item">
          <a class="breadcrumb__link" href="{{ parent_url }}">{{ parent_title }}</a>
          {%- render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-right-small', class: 'breadcrumb__separator', direction_aware: true -%}
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
        {%- if crumb_aisle != null -%}
          <li class="breadcrumb__item">
            <a class="breadcrumb__link" href="{{ crumb_aisle.url }}">{{ crumb_aisle.title }}</a>
            {%- render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-right-small', class: 'breadcrumb__separator', direction_aware: true -%}
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if crumb_format != null -%}
          <li class="breadcrumb__item">
            <a class="breadcrumb__link" href="{{ crumb_format.url }}">{{ crumb_format.title }}</a>
            {%- render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-right-small', class: 'breadcrumb__separator', direction_aware: true -%}
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- elsif request.page_type == 'article' -%}
        <li class="breadcrumb__item">
          <a class="breadcrumb__link" href="{{ blog.url }}">{{ blog.title }}</a>
          {%- render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-right-small', class: 'breadcrumb__separator', direction_aware: true -%}
        </li>
      {%- endif -%}

      <li class="breadcrumb__item">
        <span class="breadcrumb__current" aria-current="page">{{ current_title }}</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        {%- assign position = 1 -%}
        {
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": {{ position }},
          "name": {{ 'general.home' | t | json }},
          "item": "{{ shop.url }}"
        }

        {%- if parent_url != '' -%}
          {%- assign position = position | plus: 1 -%}
          ,{
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ position }},
            "name": {{ parent_title | json }},
            "item": "{{ shop.url }}{{ parent_url }}"
          }
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if request.page_type == 'product' -%}
          {%- if crumb_aisle != null -%}
            {%- assign position = position | plus: 1 -%}
            ,{
              "@type": "ListItem",
              "position": {{ position }},
              "name": {{ crumb_aisle.title | json }},
              "item": "{{ shop.url }}{{ crumb_aisle.url }}"
            }
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- if crumb_format != null -%}
            {%- assign position = position | plus: 1 -%}
            ,{
              "@type": "ListItem",
              "position": {{ position }},
              "name": {{ crumb_format.title | json }},
              "item": "{{ shop.url }}{{ crumb_format.url }}"
            }
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- elsif request.page_type == 'article' -%}
          {%- assign position = position | plus: 1 -%}
          ,{
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": {{ position }},
            "name": {{ blog.title | json }},
            "item": "{{ shop.url }}{{ blog.url }}"
          }
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- assign position = position | plus: 1 -%}
        ,{
          "@type": "ListItem",
          "position": {{ position }},
          "name": {{ current_title | json }},
          "item": {{ canonical_url | json }}
        }
      ]
    }
  </script>
{%- endif -%}
